# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Caddy reverse proxy for the multi-tenant ERP with per-client custom domains.
#
# How it works
#   • Every tenant is reachable at its own hostname (acme.erp.example.com or a
#     client's own erp.clientco.com). The app resolves the tenant from the Host
#     header (see backend/tenancy.py → resolve_tenant_from_scope).
#   • On-demand TLS: Caddy fetches a Let's Encrypt certificate the first time a
#     new host is seen — but ONLY if the `ask` endpoint approves it, so random
#     domains pointed at this server can't trigger certificate issuance.
#   • The ask endpoint is GET /api/platform/tls-check?domain=<host>, which the
#     app answers 200 for a known + VERIFIED tenant domain and 404 otherwise.
#
# Onboarding a client domain
#   1. Operator: POST /api/platform/tenants/<slug>/domains { "domain": "erp.clientco.com" }
#      → returns a TXT record to publish.
#   2. Client: add DNS  _erp-verify.erp.clientco.com  TXT  "<token>"
#   3. Operator: POST /api/platform/domains/erp.clientco.com/verify  → verified.
#   4. Client: point  erp.clientco.com  CNAME → app.erp.example.com  (or A → IP).
#   5. First request triggers Caddy → ask → cert issued → live over HTTPS.
#
# Prereqs: the app runs with TENANCY=schema and COOKIE_SECURE=true (HTTPS).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

{
	# Approve certificate issuance only for hosts the app recognises.
	on_demand_tls {
		ask http://app:8766/api/platform/tls-check
	}
	# email you@example.com   # ACME account email (recommended)
}

# Your own vendor domain + all tenant subdomains (acme.erp.example.com, …).
erp.example.com, *.erp.example.com {
	tls {
		# Wildcard needs a DNS challenge; configure your DNS provider plugin here,
		# or list explicit subdomains instead of the wildcard.
	}
	reverse_proxy app:8766
}

# Any other hostname (a client's custom domain) — gated by on-demand TLS.
https:// {
	tls {
		on_demand
	}
	reverse_proxy app:8766
}
